{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m implementing the ABI layer as architecture-neutral tail-call trampolines: each exported Rust `extern \"C\"` entry point preserves the caller’s full register/stack ABI and jumps to a namespaced backend symbol. The build script will compile the unchanged reference sources into private namespaced objects, generate one Rust `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` trampoline per exported function, and leave the two exported data symbols intact; this keeps the final cdylib self-contained and avoids symbol collisions."}}
